I read the rules written below on the mobile screen again.
It is clearly written there in official language.
"If the code is not received, then another code is sent via email."
I touch the 'email' option.
Usually, it is done exactly like this on government websites.
When the SMS does not come, then email is used.
Then I open the email app.
Right there at the top is a new message.
The expected code is in that message.
I go to the website screen again.
I write that code in the empty space there.
Then I touch the 'submit' button.
Instantly, a green checkmark is seen on the screen.
A new message is written there.
"Your profile is successfully updated."
I feel great satisfaction.
Finally, this boring task is finished.
